# Retired addresses, kept answering rather than left to the SPA fallback.
#
# The fallback is the trap: an unknown path is served index.html with a 200,
# so a dead URL silently shows the homepage and a crawler files it as another
# copy of the front page instead of dropping it. An edge redirect here is the
# mechanism that actually works — a client-side <Navigate> needs JavaScript,
# and emitting no file at all leaves the CDN serving its cached copy of the
# OLD page for as long as its cache header allows.

# The standalone pricing page is retired. Keep old shared links useful.
/pricing / 301
/pricing/ / 301

